# ArduPilot Rover skid-steering parameters for the skid_rover Gazebo model.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   `sim_vehicle.py -f rover-skid` is supposed to load skid defaults, but the
#   frame defaults only apply on a fresh EEPROM - a previous default-Rover run
#   leaves SERVO1_FUNCTION=26 (GroundSteering) / SERVO3_FUNCTION=70 (Throttle)
#   in the stored params, which do NOT match the skid_rover plugin wiring and
#   make the rover steer/curve instead of driving straight. Loading this file
#   forces the skid configuration every run.
#
# WIRING (matches gazebo/models/skid_rover/model.sdf ArduPilotPlugin):
#   SERVO1 = ThrottleLeft  (fn 73) -> plugin channel 0 -> LEFT  wheels
#   SERVO3 = ThrottleRight (fn 74) -> plugin channel 2 -> RIGHT wheels
#   ArduPilot auto-detects skid steering from the presence of ThrottleLeft +
#   ThrottleRight and mixes throttle+steering into the two outputs, so there is
#   no separate steering channel.
#   MIN/MAX pinned to 1100/1900 to match the plugin's servo_min/servo_max
#   (trim 1500 = stop, full reverse 1100, full forward 1900).
#
# USAGE
#   sim_vehicle.py -v Rover --model JSON -I1 --console --map \
#     --add-param-file=gazebo/config/rover_skid.parm

SERVO1_FUNCTION 73
SERVO3_FUNCTION 74
SERVO1_MIN 1100
SERVO1_MAX 1900
SERVO1_TRIM 1500
SERVO3_MIN 1100
SERVO3_MAX 1900
SERVO3_TRIM 1500
